title: read_secret drops data.metadata (version/destroyed/created_time)
updated: 2026-09-10T03:41:08Z
---

read_secret returns only data.data and discards data.metadata, which carries the version number, destroyed flag and created_time. Surfacing that metadata is useful (especially after a versioned read) but must not change read_secret existing return shape (the bare data hashref), which consumers (goldmine, hiplatform) depend on. This is a design decision, not a mechanical change: options include a separate method (e.g. read_secret_metadata, or a read that returns both data and metadata), an optional out-parameter, or a wantarray tuple. Needs a maintainer decision and POD. Split out from ticket 6, which delivered the version argument; this is the design half of that ticket, left for Getty to decide.
